+## 11a. Voided results
+
+A result that should never have counted is withdrawn by voiding its match
+while the tournament is still active. The match stops counting, the reason is
+kept, and the standings are rebuilt from the results that remain, so an award
+a later win only reached because of the voided one is not paid twice over.
+Nothing is subtracted: awards are decided again from an empty record, which is
+the only way the streak, the best streak and the counts stay honest.
+
+A void that leaves a player with nothing gives back an empty record stamped at
+the moment of the void. `tournament:voids` reads the ledger, one line per
+player whose total moved, and says how many points came back.
+
+The event carries the rebuilt records, so replaying the journal reaches the
+same standings the live arena is showing.
+
+## 11b. Published boards
+
+`publishLeaderboard` freezes the board an operator stands behind. Every board
+handed out afterwards measures movement against that one, so a void in between
+cannot invent movement out of a board nobody ever saw. Before the first
+publication a rank is new: no previous rank, no movement.
+
